        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.083,
            0.72,
            0.287,
            0.784
          ],
          "content": "Why do suspended particles settle in muddy water over time but not in milk?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.084,
            0.786,
            0.296,
            0.818
          ],
          "content": "How is evaporation different from boiling?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.083,
            0.82,
            0.294,
            0.914
          ],
          "content": "Why do you see bright rays of sunlight when it passes through small gaps between the leaves of a dense tree?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.319,
            0.686,
            0.89,
            0.773
          ],
          "content": "Have you ever wondered how sweet, white crystals of sugar are obtained from tall, green sugarcane plants? Or how do doctors detect diseases like malaria using just a few drops of blood? Many such everyday activities are made possible by techniques based on the fascinating science of separating mixtures."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.328,
            0.777,
            0.405,
            0.814
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_0_image_11.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.321,
            0.774,
            0.891,
            0.895
          ],
          "content": "Grade 6 You have learnt about mixtures and some simple CuriosityChapter 9 methods to separate them. In this chapter, you will **explore** mixtures in greater depth, including their properties, behaviour and the various techniques used to separate them. From industrial processes like sugar production to life-saving medical tests, the separation of mixtures plays a crucial role in our daily lives."
        }
      ]
    }
